<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Bremen Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Bremen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Council republic in the port city of Bremen in early 1919, suppressed after a few weeks by government troops.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-revolution-of-1918-1919">November revolution</a> of 1918, workers' and soldiers' councils took power in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen">Bremen</a>. On 10 January 1919, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartacist-uprising">Spartacist rising</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, left-wing radicals and Communists proclaimed a Soviet Republic, dissolving the city's senate and parliament.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The council government, dominated by Communists and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/independent-social-democratic-party-of-germany">Independent Socialists</a>, controlled the city for less than a month. It faced shortages of money and food, as banks refused credit, and opposition from the middle classes and moderate Social Democrats. Its leaders tried to negotiate with the national government but refused to disarm.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 4 February 1919 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">Freikorps</a> Division Gerstenberg, sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-noske">Gustav Noske</a>, stormed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen">Bremen</a>. About 80 people died, and the Soviet Republic ended. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> resumed as a city-state within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bremen-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Bremen Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bremen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bremer Räterepublik</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=bremen-soviet-republic" aria-label="Bremen Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4877 350 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bremen Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5197 606L5197 606M5197 606L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5197 606h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5197 606h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5197 606h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bremen. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=bremen-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
